cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "madrid-ai-ethics: systems friction and outsider impact in civic digital services (research notes)"
message: "If you cite this work, please cite the repository and treat claims as reflective research notes, not validated experimental results."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhao
    given-names: Jade
    email: jadexzhao@outlook.com
    affiliation: "Indiana University Luddy"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zhao-langxi/madrid-ai-ethics"
url: "https://github.com/zhao-langxi/madrid-ai-ethics"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-08-06"
abstract: >
  Public research notes locking a falsifiable claim about systems friction
  disadvantaging outsiders in civic digital services, with a pattern library
  from a Madrid study-abroad semester, an Outsider Impact Review template,
  and a reflective essay on AI ethics in public services (accountability,
  auditability, human override). Not an EU AI Act compliance project.
  Reflective practice only; no fabricated metrics or controlled-study results.
keywords:
  - systems friction
  - digital government
  - language access
  - public-interest AI
  - accountability
  - reflective practice
